Description: Ozone/X11: Reuse the main GL display for native pixmap import
 Backport of the upstream fix. NativePixmapEGLX11Binding created its own
 EGLDisplay via a visual-less eglGetDisplay(), which on drivers that cannot
 initialise a desktop-GL display (v3d) left the pixmap unbound, so X11 video
 decoded at full rate but rendered as a flat white rectangle. Upstream hit the
 same code from a different direction - a second DisplayGLX corrupting later GL
 work on ANGLE GL bots - and fixed it by reusing the process-wide GLDisplayEGL,
 which also lets the redundant eglInitialize() go.
 .
 Drop this patch once we move to a Chromium that contains it (>= 152.0.7968).
Origin: upstream, https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/3900f0b991abc
Applied-Upstream: 3900f0b991abc
Last-Update: 2026-08-03

